<h1>SecureU — Free 24/7 Online Hosting Guide</h1>
<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> How to get a free, permanent public HTTPS link for your teacher and external evaluation.</p>
<hr/>

<h2>Method 1: Netlify Drop (Fastest — 15 Seconds, Zero Setup)</h2>
<div class="callout">
  <p><strong>Steps:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open your browser and navigate to: <a href="https://app.netlify.com/drop">https://app.netlify.com/drop</a></li>
    <li>In File Explorer, open your project folder: <code>C:\Users\Hariprasad\Videos\JAVA PROJECT</code></li>
    <li>Locate the <strong><code>web</code></strong> folder.</li>
    <li><strong>Drag and drop the <code>web</code> folder</strong> into the upload area on Netlify Drop.</li>
    <li>Your site is instantly live! Netlify will display your permanent public URL (e.g., <code>https://secureu-project.netlify.app</code>).</li>
    <li>Send this link directly to your teacher.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<h2>Method 2: Vercel (Professional Cloud Hosting)</h2>
<div class="callout">
  <ol>
    <li>Push your project to GitHub.</li>
    <li>Log into <a href="https://vercel.com">https://vercel.com</a> with your GitHub account.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Add New Project</strong>, select your repository.</li>
    <li>The pre-configured <code>vercel.json</code> will automatically route the site. Click <strong>Deploy</strong>.</li>
    <li>Your live link will be generated: <code>https://secureu.vercel.app</code>.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<h2>Template Message to Send Your Teacher</h2>
<div class="callout">
  <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Java Project / DBMS Lab Submission — SecureU Portal Demo</p>
  <p>Dear Professor,</p>
  <p>Here is the live demo link for our project <strong>SecureU — Student Safety & Grievance Redressal Portal</strong>:</p>
  <p><strong>Live Demo Link:</strong> <code>https://your-app-name.netlify.app</code></p>
  <p><strong>Demo Test Accounts:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Student Login:</strong> Click <em>"Abhinav (Student)"</em> on the login card to file complaints with live image attachments and view the resolution timeline.</li>
    <li><strong>Warden Login:</strong> Click <em>"Priya (Warden)"</em> to review hostel complaints, update status, and view attachments.</li>
    <li><strong>HOD Login:</strong> Click <em>"Suresh (HOD)"</em> to view department complaints and resolution analytics charts.</li>
    <li><strong>Database Inspector:</strong> Click the <em>"SQL Database"</em> button in the top navigation to view the live relational tables.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<hr/>
<p style="text-align: center; color: #737373; font-size: 9pt;">SecureU — Student Safety & Grievance Redressal Portal</p>

